# Docs with code (standing rule)

When changing **backend API** or **TS domain core**, update docs **in the same change** — not “later”.

## Backend / API v2

| Change | Doc |
|---|---|
| New/changed HTTP route, DTO, auth | `docs/api-v2/services/<service>.md` (+ OpenAPI stub if present) |
| New service or contour | `docs/api-v2/OVERVIEW.md` |
| Kafka topic / event shape | `docs/api-v2/KAFKA.md` |
| Cross-cutting architecture | `docs/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` |

Keep contracts **contract-first**: paths, request/response shapes, ownership, out-of-scope. Match what FE/`core-api` will call.

## Frontend / TS core

| Change | Doc |
|---|---|
| New/changed `@matchwear/core-*` API | `packages/js/<pkg>/README.md` (exports, examples, ports) |
| New domain package | README + row in `docs/FRONTEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| New `core-api` live/mock port | short note in package README or `docs/api-v2` link |

`core-*` stays **no React**; docs describe pure functions / controllers / ports.

## Always

- Ship doc updates with the feature PR/commit that introduces the surface
- Prefer short accurate docs over long aspirational ones
- If behavior diverges from docs, fix docs in the same edit

## Don't

- Leave new `/v2/...` endpoints undocumented
- Add public `core-*` exports without README mention
- Dump secrets, tokens, or full env values into docs
